# Fugue No. 3 in C-sharp major, BWV 848 (J. S. Bach, WTC I)
#
# Character: bright, sparkling and good-humoured, three voices in 4/4.
# The subject starts on the upbeat with a little turning figure
# (G#, A# G# F# G#, then up to E# and C#) and a leaping second half
# (E# C#' D# B#' C#): it should dance, light and clean, never rushed.
# The episodes are canonic chains of tied suspensions over a running
# bass, a texture Bach comes back to three times.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 98. 55 bars of 4/4 is 220 quarters. Per-fugue track
# times (MusicBrainz track lists): Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1998) 2:14,
# about 98; Rosalyn Tureck (2002 issue) 2:11, about 101; Sviatoslav
# Richter 2:05 and Glenn Gould 2:04, both about 106. 98 is the
# unhurried end of that range, so the sixteenths stay clear on the chip.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score; bar 1 begins with a dotted-quarter
# rest, the subject enters on beat 2 and a half):
#   1-7    Exposition, C-sharp major: subject top (1-3), answer in the
#          alto (3-5, the lowest voice until the bass enters), subject
#          in the bass (5-7).
#   7-10   Episode 1: suspensions in the upper voices over running
#          sixteenths in the bass, a falling sequence.
#   10-12  Answer in the top, cadence in G-sharp major (12).
#   12-14  Short link.
#   14-16  Subject in the bass in A-sharp minor.
#   16-19  Episode 2: episode 1 again with the parts exchanged.
#   19-22  Subject in the alto (middle voice), E-sharp minor; cadence
#          in E-sharp minor on beat 3 of bar 22.
#   22-25  Episode on the subject head, falling.
#   25-26  Answer in the top (G-sharp major).
#   27-28  Subject in the alto, back in C-sharp major.
#   28-31  Episode with E and B naturals, a darker minor colouring.
#   31-34  Arpeggio sequence falling by fifths; cadence in C-sharp
#          major, bar 34 beat 3.
#   35-41  Two-voice episode (the bass rests nine bars): the head in
#          sequence, a long trilled G-sharp in the top (38).
#   42-48  The exposition returns almost note for note: top (42-44),
#          alto (44-46), bass (46-48).
#   48-51  Episode 1 once more.
#   52-53  Last subject, in the top, C-sharp major.
#   53-55  Coda and final cadence.
# The entry list was checked against the MIDI with a pattern search on
# the subject's turning figure. The bar 27 alto entry shares notes with
# the bass in unison, so the MIDI shows it imperfectly.

tempo 98

dyn 1 mf           # bars 1-11: the exposition and first episode, bright
dyn 12 mp          # bars 12-22: after the G-sharp cadence the music
                   # turns to the minor keys (A-sharp minor, E-sharp
                   # minor): a quieter manual
dyn 22.5 mf        # bars 22-34: after the E-sharp minor cadence, back
                   # toward the tonic
dyn 35 mp          # bars 35-41: after the C-sharp cadence the bass drops
                   # out; a lighter, two-voice passage
dyn 42 f           # bars 42-55: the exposition returns, full

lead 1-2 top       # subject, top
lead 3-4 bottom    # answer in the alto, the lowest voice until bar 5
lead 5-6 bottom    # subject, bass
lead 10-11 top     # answer, top, toward G-sharp major
lead 14-15 bottom  # subject, bass, A-sharp minor
lead 19-20 mid     # subject in the alto, E-sharp minor: the hidden one
lead 25-26 top     # answer, top
lead 27 mid        # subject in the alto, C-sharp major
lead 44-45 mid     # recapitulation: the answer in the alto, now between
                   # the outer voices
lead 46-47 bottom  # recapitulation: subject, bass
lead 52-53 top     # last subject, top

rit 2 0.75         # last two bars into the final chord
